==Japanese==
{{ja-kanjitab|おこな|yomi=kun|alt=行なう}}

===Etymology===
From classical yodan ([[四段活用]]) verb {{ja-r|行ふ|おこなふ}}, possibly formed from {{com-ja|おこ|pos1=from {{ja-r|起く|おく}}||なふ|pos2=verb-forming suffix}}. However, the suffix nafu usually attaches on nominal roots, not other verb stems, making the theorized suffixation unusual.

